codex
The authoritative matrix contains concurrency attacks, but its `submit` race test releases the gate before proving all callers entered the factory, so it can pass without exercising the check then register window. The committed code also records a cancel receipt only after releasing the per run cancel lock. I’m using deterministic barriers to verify both windows against `ee39270`, then I’ll run the accepted suites and shape locks for the unaffected requirements.
